Today I solved leetcode question number 1669: Merge In Between Linked Lists.
Description: It states that we are given two linked lists, list1 and list2, and we are given two values 'a' and 'b'.
              We must insert list2 in between those values of list1.
              eg- If list1=[1,2,3,4,5,6,7], list2=[11,12,13,14], a='2' and b='4'
                  So our output should be ans=[1,2,11,12,13,14,6,7]
              We must replace values at location 'a' to 'b' with list2 in list1.

Solution: So I took 2 variables. With 'start' being head of list2 and 'end' being ending node of list2.
          Then I took a pointer named 'temp'. It points to head of list1.
          And I took an integer 'n'=0.
          Our goal was simple, when we reached the location 'a-1' we will point that node to 'start' variable.
          And when we reached 'b+1' we will point next of 'end' variable to that node.
          Otherwise we will just increase 'n' and move 'temp'.
